# diff-kernels' known differences: `<name> <max ulps | any> <reason>`.
# A name is a std_kernels function (or a gm function, for the math swap)
# whose answer differs from the old one; `any` is a difference that is not
# a number of ulps (NaN against a number, a sign, a text). Each line says
# which side the f128 reference sides with. A line whose name agrees fails
# the run: remove it. Every difference below is the gm -> Gompute 2.0.0
# swap (lib/TODO.md §11.8); every other port is bit-identical.
#
# Gompute against gm (`math.zig`), judged by the f128 reference:
atan 1 Gompute's atan is std's VECTOR body on every target (gm: std's scalar body on the host); 20771/100676 differ; f128 sides with gm (old max 0.678 ulp, new max 1.235 ulp, old closer 20769 times)
atan2 2 via atan; 12312/100676 differ; f128 sides with gm (old max 1.311, new max 1.951 ulp, old closer 10271 times, new 2041)
cosh 1 Gompute's softCosh, not std's cosh64; 8276/100676 differ; f128 sides with Gompute (old max 1.146, new max 0.964 ulp, new closer 8197 times)
sinh 1 Gompute's softSinh near overflow (|x| ~ 710); 5/100676 differ; f128 sides with Gompute (old max 0.871, new max 0.654 ulp, new closer 3 of 5)
log10 1 Gompute's log10 (log's hi/lo pair times 1/ln10 as a double-double), not musl's e_log10; 2/100676 differ; f128 sides with Gompute (old max 0.505, new max 0.496 ulp)
# The kernels over them (old text and lib/kernels called gm or std.math):
math.zDevAtan 1 = atan
math.zDevSinh 1 = sinh
math.zDevCosh 1 = cosh
math.zAtan2 2 = atan2 (the value; its lanes are unchanged)
math.zLog10 1 = log10
math.zLog10D 1 = log10
fold.math.atan 2 = atan (the fold's old atan was std.math.atan's scalar body)
fold.math.atan2 2 = atan2
fold.math.cosh 1 = cosh
fold.math.log 1 = log10 (VAMS `log` is base 10)
ac.Ac.atan 1 = atan
ac.Ac.sinh 2 = sinh's value, and cosh in its lanes (each lane is a product with cosh)
ac.Ac.cosh 2 = cosh's value, and sinh in its lanes
